{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.no_scaling_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.no_scaling_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L132-L138","doc":"**The substrate case.** The dilation the W1 route asks for is `z ↦ q₀²z` with\n`q₀ ≈ 1.10998`, so `l = q₀² > 1`; no such `l` preserves the branch locus. Stated\nfor any real `l > 1` so that no numerical value enters the Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.no_scaling_of_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.no_scaling_of_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L125-L130","doc":"**No nontrivial dilation preserves the branch locus.** Contrapositive form:\na dilation by `l ≠ 1` cannot send the branch sextic to a multiple of itself, so\n(by the covering argument in this file's header) it admits no lift to `Σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.dilation_scaling_rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.dilation_scaling_rigid","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L105-L123","doc":"**Scaling rigidity of the branch locus.** If the branch sextic precomposed\nwith a dilation `z ↦ l·z` is a constant multiple of itself, then `l = 1` and the\nconstant is `1`.\n\nThe constant term gives `16 = c·16`, hence `c = 1`; the linear term then gives\n`24·l = 24`, hence `l = 1`. Characteristic zero is used only to invert those two\nintegers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.C_mul_branchSexticPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.C_mul_branchSexticPoly","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L92-L99","doc":"A constant multiple of the sextic, in the same normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.branchSexticPoly_comp_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.branchSexticPoly_comp_scale","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L83-L90","doc":"Precomposition with the dilation `z ↦ l·z`, coefficients read off. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.eval_branchSexticPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.eval_branchSexticPoly","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L77-L81","doc":"The polynomial avatar evaluates to the corpus's branch sextic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.branchSexticPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity.branchSexticPoly","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DilationBranchLocusRigidity.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The **branch-locus sextic as a polynomial**, `16X⁶+24X⁵+35X⁴+50X³+35X²+24X+16`.\nThe polynomial avatar of `QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.branchSextic`; see\n`eval_branchSexticPoly`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}